    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6369A\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the village law and the public officers law, in relation\nto authorizing the village of Riverside to hire a village\nclerk/treasurer and code enforcement officer who is not a resident of\nsuch village\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nAuthorizes the village of Riverside to hire a village clerk/treasurer\nand code enforcement officer who is not a resident of such village.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSECTION 1: Amends Section 3-300 of the village law to add a new subdivi-\nsion allowing the village of riverside, Steuben County to hire a person\nto fill the position of clerk/treasurer and code enforcement officer\nthat is not a resident of the village.\n\nSECTION 2: Amends section 3 the public officer's law to add a new subdi-\nvision. allowing a person who is not a resident. of the village of\nriverside, Steuben County to fill and perform the functions and duties\nof village clerk/treasurer and code enforcement officer.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIt is becoming extremely difficult for small rural communities to fill\nvacancies that occur in local governments. The village of riverside is\nno exception and with population of about 490 people, the task is daunt-\ning. The need to open up the geographic boundaries in their search for a\nqualified candidate to fill the positions of village clerk/treasurer and\ncode enforcement officer is critical to the operation of the village.\nThe proximity to the Chemung County line is about 6.5 miles and this\nbill Will provide the village With the increased population from Which\nto search for the vacant position of village clerk/treasurer and code\nenforcement officer.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
